  "explanation": "The provided documents contain two distinct narratives regarding Johannes Moreelse's work locations. Document 1 (D1) explicitly states he 'worked in Rome' and describes his arrival there in 1627 (D1S4, D1S8). Document 2 (D2) explicitly states he worked in 'Paris', describing his atelier in the Latin Quarter and his status as a fixture in the Parisian art scene starting in 1625 (D2S2, D2S4). Both 'Rome' and 'Paris' are directly supported as work locations in their respective source texts. Other candidates like 'Utrecht' (birth place), 'Galleria Borghese' (museum housing a work), and 'Latin Quarter' (neighborhood within Paris) are either incorrect roles (birth place vs work location) or incidental details rather than the primary city of work requested."
